00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.607
And then it goes,

00:02:02.607 --> 00:02:04.440
♪ It seems awful to me ♪

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.336
And then I go,

00:02:05.336 --> 00:02:08.504
♪ It seems awful to me ♪

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:13.170
(Kelly laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.243
- You're officially my favorite guest.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.538
- I do believe-

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:20.668
(machine beeps)

00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:23.430
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.300
- Okay wait,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.510
first musical icon who had you starstruck.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.980
Oh so you met them, so...

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:29.910
- Yeah.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.274
- Who was yours?

00:02:31.274 --> 00:02:32.658
- Bob Dylan.

00:02:32.658 --> 00:02:34.770
- Whoa.
(audience gasps)

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.810
That's a huge one.
(audience applauds)

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.510
- I know, the story is even better.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.640
I'm in New York City, I'm working.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.840
I walk into an elevator
that's the size of a shoebox.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.400
- Like Europe, yep.
- Only three people

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.240
can fit in there.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.003
And I look up, it's Bob Dylan.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.870
He says...
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.030
No and then your heart
goes (explosion sound)

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.530
and all these things happen.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.027
And then he says,

00:03:01.027 --> 00:03:02.820
"You know Bob, huh?"

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.807
Bob De Niro.
- Yeah.

00:03:04.807 --> 00:03:06.510
- "You were in that movie",

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.707
he says to me, and I'm like,

00:03:08.707 --> 00:03:10.266
"And you're Bob Dylan."

00:03:10.266 --> 00:03:12.060
(audience laughs)

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.167
And so then my little brain was like,

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:16.860
"Say hi, how are you?"

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:17.910
Because I was gonna faint.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.440
And then I got to the van driver
who was taking me to work,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:27.440
and because Bob Dylan
meant such a huge thing.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.910
I listened to this song for months on end

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.010
called "She Belongs to Me",

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.360
through one of the hardest times

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.550
of my entire life when I was 22.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.383
- Yeah.

00:03:36.383 --> 00:03:39.030
- And so his lyrics were biblical to me.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.310
They really helped me a lot.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.143
The opening line is,

00:03:42.143 --> 00:03:43.710
"She's got everything she needs,

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.500
she's an artist, she don't look back"

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.530
And, oh my god (laughs)

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.470
Do not cry.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.444
- You're not crying, you're good.

00:03:50.444 --> 00:03:51.277
You're not crying.
- Anyway,

00:03:51.277 --> 00:03:53.137
I get in the van, I say,

00:03:53.137 --> 00:03:55.080
"I just met Bob Dylan."

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.540
And then I promptly start sobbing,

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.160
and I was like, that poor man.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.200
I had enough sense to like leave him,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.390
not cry to him but,

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.650
it was really special.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.630
- I think he probably
thought that was cool.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.040
I think it's sad when you meet people

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.840
that you love or they've affected you

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.370
in some way and you
aren't touched like that.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.203
- Yes.

00:04:12.203 --> 00:04:13.590
- I think that that's a sad thing.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.800
Maybe you're too jaded at that point.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.810
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.100
- We're too cool,

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.079
there's certain people-
- I've never been too cool.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:20.550
(Kelly laughs)
- I love that.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.110
Same.
- Ever.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.460
My story's not gonna,

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.960
I just don't feel like,
- What's yours?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.300
- I mean, I have several that are,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.490
the people definitely are comparable.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.770
I just mean like, that
was an intense situation.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.180
Like that you were alone with that person.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.013
- Yeah.
- But I,

00:04:34.013 --> 00:04:37.230
I feel like might've been literally

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.660
like my favorite singer on planet Earth.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.730
It's like a tie with
she and Trisha Yearwood,

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.350
but Aretha Franklin.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.850
And it was like, but here's the thing.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.530
It wasn't private.
- Excuse me,

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.291
Bob Dylan, Aretha Franklin
- But it wasn't private.

00:04:48.291 --> 00:04:49.290
No no no.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.610
But it wasn't private.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:51.690
It was just, it was literally,

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.080
we were both at this event
and I believe it was Randy,

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.017
Randy Jackson who was like,

00:04:56.017 --> 00:04:57.150
"Hey, you gotta come say hi",

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:57.983
and I was like,

00:04:57.983 --> 00:04:58.816
"No, I don't."

00:04:58.816 --> 00:04:59.960
I was like,

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.950
"I do not. I will look from afar."

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.660
I don't do well with people.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.493
- Yes.

00:05:04.493 --> 00:05:05.326
- I become an idiot.

00:05:05.326 --> 00:05:07.110
And I, yeah, just silly.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.860
And so he got me up there and I was like,

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.110
and she came off stage and she
literally was so nice to me.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:16.140
But it was so awesome to see as an artist,

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.380
like a young artist
watching a complete legend,

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.080
and she came off and she
could not get out of her head.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.047
She was like,

00:05:23.047 --> 00:05:25.230
"Man, was it, it's, I felt like my vocals,

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.063
I couldn't hear the vo-"

00:05:26.063 --> 00:05:26.896
And it was like,

00:05:26.896 --> 00:05:28.470
"Oh my god, this is like
me coming off stage."

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.303
- [Juliette] Yep.

00:05:29.303 --> 00:05:30.600
- I was like, "Oh so this
is never gonna change."

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.160
- Yeah.
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.177
- I was like, she came
off and she was like,

00:05:33.177 --> 00:05:35.010
"I felt like I could have done better,

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.720
like, it was like my vocal, I don't know.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.740
Did you feel the room was weird?"

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.090
And I was like, "Oh my God."

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.950
And it was like the Ghost
of Christmas Future.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.637
Like, I was like, I was like,

00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:43.470
"I'm never gonna

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.600
not be this person"
- It never gets better.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.640
- Like a seasoned pro, nope.
- I know!

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.660
- You're still gonna head-

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.190
- I know, it's like still gonna, yeah.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.170
But it kind of made me feel awesome,

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.600
like as a young artist
to watch this legend

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.134
and make me not feel crazy sometimes.

00:05:56.134 --> 00:05:57.930
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.451
Anyway, give it up for
Juliette Lewis everyone.

00:05:59.451 --> 00:06:01.235
